1 NOTE Key facts Birthplace: Pakistan; naturalized U.S. citizen Education: Harvard University alumnus Residence: Rancho Mirage, California / Los Angeles Partner: Scott Murray Notable roles: Chair, Board of Advisors – Hammer
2 CONC Museum; National Finance Chair – Will Rollins for Congress Early life and education Raised in Karachi in a family central to Pakistan’s architectural preservation movement, Lari later studied at Harvard College, where he
2 CONC served as Class Marshal. His parents’ work in heritage and social architecture shaped his interest in the intersection of design, culture, and civic responsibility. Advocacy and recognition Lari has spoken publicly about
2 CONC LGBTQ+ equality, notably challenging discriminatory U.S. customs policies against same-sex couples in 2011 . He continues to work across philanthropic, political, and cultural networks promoting inclusion and
2 CONC sustainability. Publications With his mother, he co-authored The Dual City: Karachi During the Raj, a landmark study of Karachi’s colonial-era urban history
